<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 June, from 363 to 2007.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">363 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,663 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Roman army proclaims Jovian emperor after Julian's death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Emperor Julian was killed in battle on his Persian expedition, the Roman army declared Jovian, of the imperial bodyguard, his successor. Jovian then made a peace that let the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-ii">Shapur II</a> recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nisibis">Nisibis</a> and other territories.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-emperor">Julian</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rome" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">678 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,348 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Agatho begins his pontificate as bishop of Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Agatho became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, serving until his death in 681. During his tenure the Sixth Ecumenical Council was convened to deal with monothelitism, and he is venerated as a saint by both the Catholic and Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> churches.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Eastern Orthodox Church</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1556">1556 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">470 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Stratford Martyrs are burned for their Protestant beliefs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eleven men and two women, the Stratford Martyrs, were burned at the stake together for their Protestant beliefs during the Marian persecutions, at Stratford-le-Bow or Stratford, Essex, both near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1743 CE <span class="tih-ago">283 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George II leads his army to victory at Dettingen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a>, an allied army under George II beat the French in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. It was the last time a reigning British monarch commanded troops in battle.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1844">1844 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">182 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mormon founder Joseph Smith is killed by a mob</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Militiamen stormed the jail in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, where Smith and his brother Hyrum were held, and shot them dead. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigham-young">Brigham Young</a> later led most of his followers west to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sailors mutiny aboard the battleship Potemkin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crew of the Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a> battleship rose against their officers after a dispute over rotten meat. The mutiny became a symbol of the 1905 Revolution, later immortalised by Eisenstein.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1950">1950 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UN Security Council calls on members to defend South Korea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Resolution 83 recommended that members help <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> repel the North's attack. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> was boycotting the Council and could not veto it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2007">2007 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">19 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gordon Brown succeeds Tony Blair as Prime Minister</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After ten years as Chancellor, Gordon Brown became Prime Minister. His premiership was dominated by the global financial crisis of 2008.</p></div></li></ol>
